    <statement><p>Use the chain rule to find <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s}</m> and
 <m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t}</m>, where 
<me>z = e^{xy}\tan y, x = 5 s + 4 t, y = \frac{4 s}{4 t}</me></p>
<p>First the pieces:</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial x} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial y} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial x}{\partial s} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/>
<m>\frac{\partial x}{\partial t} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial y}{\partial s} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0005"/>
<m>\frac{\partial y}{\partial t} =</m><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p>And putting it all together:</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial s} = 
\frac{\partial z}{\partial x}\frac{\partial x}{\partial s} + 
\frac{\partial z}{\partial y}\frac{\partial y}{\partial s}</m>
and
<m>\frac{\partial z}{\partial t} =
\frac{\partial z}{\partial x}\frac{\partial x}{\partial t} + 
\frac{\partial z}{\partial y}\frac{\partial y}{\partial t}</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y\tan\mathopen{}\left(y\right)\exp\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\exp\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)\sec^{2}\mathopen{}\left(y\right)+\tan\mathopen{}\left(y\right)x\exp\mathopen{}\left(xy\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{4}{4t}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-4s}{4t^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
